traceability.evidence:
normalizeCommentLine implementation does not perform any backtick/inline-code filtering:

File: src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-format-internal.ts

export function normalizeCommentLine(rawLine: string): string {
  const trimmed = rawLine.trim();
  if (!trimmed) {
    return "";
  }

  const annotationMatch = trimmed.match(/@story\b|@req\b|@supports\b/);
  if (!annotationMatch || annotationMatch.index === undefined) {
    const withoutLeadingStar = trimmed.replace(/^\*\s?/, "");
    return withoutLeadingStar;
  }

  return trimmed.slice(annotationMatch.index);
}

There is no logic here to strip backtick-wrapped content or replace it with spaces as required by REQ-IGNORE-INLINE-CODE and REQ-PRESERVE-BOUNDARIES.,Searches show no reference to the new requirement IDs or inline-code/backtick behavior in implementation or tests:

- grep -R REQ-IGNORE-INLINE-CODE -n src tests docs
  -> only hit is in docs/stories/024.0-DEV-IGNORE-INLINE-CODE-REFS.story.md (the story itself)

- search_file_content on src/rules/helpers/valid-annotation-format-internal.ts for "inline code" and "REQ-IGNORE-INLINE-CODE" -> no matches

- grep -R ` (backtick character) src
  -> hits are general string templates and documentation comments (e.g. in prefer-implements-annotation.ts, require-test-traceability-helpers.ts), but none in normalizeCommentLine or related comment-normalization logic.

- grep -R 024.0-DEV-IGNORE-INLINE-CODE-REFS tests src docs
  -> only in docs/stories/024.0-DEV-IGNORE-INLINE-CODE-REFS.story.md and docs/stories/plugin-developer-story.map.md, not in any test or source file implementing behavior.,Existing tests for valid-annotation-format and related helpers do not cover inline-code/backtick cases or reference Story 024.0:

- tests/rules/valid-annotation-format.test.ts header references stories 005.0, 007.0, 010.1, 010.2, 022.0 but not 024.0. It has no test cases whose code strings include backtick-wrapped @story/@req/@supports.

- search_file_content on tests/rules/valid-annotation-format.test.ts for "`@story`" returned no matches.

- grep -R "backtick" src tests docs failed (no semantic references to backtick handling outside of a few generic comments).

This means there are no unit tests for the new behavior required by this story (Core Functionality, Common Patterns, Real Annotations Detected, Multi-Line Support).,Documentation update required by the story is missing:

- The only documentation mentioning this behavior is the story itself:
  docs/stories/024.0-DEV-IGNORE-INLINE-CODE-REFS.story.md (defines REQ-IGNORE-INLINE-CODE, REQ-PRESERVE-BOUNDARIES, REQ-CENTRALIZED-FILTER and the Technical Approach for normalizeCommentLine).

- No other docs (e.g., README, user-docs, or rule-level docs/comments around normalizeCommentLine) describe backtick/inline-code filtering behavior.

Thus the "Documentation: Comment normalization behavior documented to explain inline code filtering" acceptance criterion is not met.,All existing tests currently pass (jest --ci --bail --verbose completed with 39 test suites, 299 tests, all passing), but this only satisfies the "No Regression" criterion in isolation; it does not demonstrate the new behavior exists because there are no tests targeting inline-code/backtick scenarios or Story 024.0. The green test run therefore cannot be used as evidence that this story’s functional criteria are implemented.
